  "reviewed_execution_text": "# Banking execution record\n\nTask: owner-authorized SC2--SC5 banking and a proposed next campaign only.\nStart2026-09-07 about03:49UTC; baseline ed2f7432f068aa7a72628382b890596b3efba06a,\ngrok synchronized by the mandatory checkout/fetch/ff-only pull sequence.\nInitial tracked worktree clean;46 unrelated untracked status entries preserved.\nMain runtime model UNKNOWN. No claim of different-model/human verification.\n\n## Scope, method and history\n\nThe main read the on-disk startup chain in its bounded order and gave the\norientation before file mutation. Verifier-before-record, no-shortcuts,\ncompleteness-map and solution-space protocols required exact source ownership,\nexplicit quantifiers, retained failure evidence and separate-context review.\nThey supplied no scientific premise. No new scientific campaign or solve began.\n\nThe main read all four candidate arguments, their REVIEW_RECORD files, direct\nreviews, SC5 focused review, prior G353--G356 banking procedure and G355/G356\narguments. It read the exact load-bearing registry rows and G321/G332/G335\naudit reports for the proposal. No protected payload or external archive read.\nCurrent tracking updates are additive banking status, not a manuscript update.\n\nSubtasks explicitly bounded by the repository review protocol:\n- /root/sc_banking_integration: only registry, existing premise verifier,\n  self-contained startup tests and integration evidence. No scientific repair.\n- /root/sc_banking_fidelity: fresh separate context, source-first scope\n  reconstruction, direct banking/proposal/integration fidelity review and\n  bounded preservation/replay checks. Not a new blind reproof of all science.\n\nThe original SC2/3/4 direct scientific reviews used0/1 post-review repairs.\nSC4's symbolic structural-equality correction preceded freeze and is retained.\nSC5 used1/1 reviewed regression repair after a REAL reject-all-nonzero false\npass. Original analytic argument and sources st